      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Sarasota Springs began as a post‑World War II subdivision along Bee Ridge Road in 1955, with homes priced at $6,995 and lots at $695.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sarasota_springs_florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1920s Florida land boom spurred speculative real‑estate investments that shaped the early development of what would become Sarasota Springs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sarasota_springs_florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 1763 Spanish sheepskin map labels the area across present‑day Bradenton and Sarasota as “Zarazote,” marking the earliest recorded reference to the locale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sarasota_springs_florida",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "At Little Salt Spring, excavations uncovered a 12,000‑year‑old wooden stake, a 7,000‑year‑old greenstone pendant, and a carved atlatl, alongside human remains and impaled tortoise shells.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sarasota_springs_florida",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Spanish explorers first noted the Sarasota region in the 18th century, with early charts labeling it as “Boca Sarazota” and later variants.",
